<title>USA: Jacksonville Electric eyes $222 mln refunding.</title>
<headline>Jacksonville Electric eyes $222 mln refunding.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-02-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Jacksonville Electric Authority, Fla., plans a $222 million refunding bond sale for St. Johns River Power Park System, according to the preliminary official statement.</p>
<p>Lehman Brothers is senior manager for the offering.</p>
<p>Moody's Investors Service has confirmed the Aa1 rating on JEA's St. John's River Power Park revenue bonds in conjunction with a refunding expected through negotiation the week of Feb. 24.</p>
<p>--U.S. Municipal Desk, 212-859-1650</p>
</text>
